Resolve declared outputs against what the build says it produced

out_static_libs has to name library files exactly, and the name a build
produces is not knowable when the rule is written. Two cases bite.

The default is wrong for CMake on unix. With nothing declared, the rule
expects lib_name + ".a", so a cmake(name = "fmt") target declares fmt.a
while CMake produces libfmt.a, and the action fails in every compilation
mode:

  ERROR: output 'fmt/lib/fmt.a' was not created
  ERROR: Foreign Cc - CMake: Building fmt failed: not all outputs were
         created or valid

Debug builds rename further. rules_foreign_cc sets CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug
itself for -c dbg, and projects append a postfix in that configuration
through CMAKE_DEBUG_POSTFIX or a variable of their own, so libfmt.a
becomes libfmtd.a. Pinning the postfix off does not help either: an empty
cache entry already means "omit this variable", so the empty string
cannot be expressed.

Bazel's contract is that a declared output exists when the action ends,
not that it is named whatever the underlying tool chose. So ask the build
rather than guess. A codemodel-v2 query is written before configure, and
each target's reply carries nameOnDisk, so a declared fmt.a or libfmt.a
resolves through target fmt to whatever that target became.

Guessing is not good enough here. fmt builds both fmt and fmt-c, and only
fmt passes through the helper that sets DEBUG_POSTFIX, so a Debug tree
holds libfmtd.a beside an unpostfixed libfmt-c.a. A libfmt*.a glob cannot
tell which is a renamed libfmt.a, and a postfix candidate list only
happens to work because nothing declared fmt-c. Asking the build makes it
structural.

When no target claims a declared name the pass fails the script, so the
build log reaches the console with a list of what was produced. Bazel's
own error names only the file that is missing. Builds that leave no
reply, such as make or ninja, take the same path.

The fragment is identical across the four platforms, using only test,
grep, cut, find and cp, so macOS needs no realpath special case.

diff --git a/foreign_cc/private/cmake_script.bzl b/foreign_cc/private/cmake_script.bzl
--- a/foreign_cc/private/cmake_script.bzl
+++ b/foreign_cc/private/cmake_script.bzl
@@ -174,6 +174,11 @@
 
     directory = "$$EXT_BUILD_ROOT$$/" + root
 
+    # Ask CMake to describe the build system it is about to generate. The reply
+    # names each target's artifact on disk, which is how a declared output can
+    # be satisfied when a configuration postfix renamed it.
+    script.append("mkdir -p .cmake/api/v1/query && :> .cmake/api/v1/query/codemodel-v2")
+
     script.append("##enable_tracing##")
 
     # Configure the CMake generate command
